# NGS Assay Performance Analysis

## Project Overview

This project investigates how sequencing depth, read quality, and bioinformatics methods influence the reliability of detecting genetic variants using next-generation sequencing (NGS).

The goal is to develop reproducible computational workflows combining Python programming, statistical modeling, and genomic data analysis.

## Initial Research Question

How does sequencing depth affect the probability of detecting a low-frequency genetic variant?

## Planned Methods

- Simulate variant-supporting reads using binomial probability models.
- Evaluate detection sensitivity across sequencing depths and variant allele frequencies.
- Investigate sequencing errors and minimum-read detection thresholds.
- Compare simulation results against theoretical predictions.
- Extend the analysis to publicly available genomic sequencing datasets.

## Tools

Python, NumPy, pandas, SciPy, Matplotlib, and R.

## Project Status

Early development — initial simulation and statistical modeling.

## Scope

This is an exploratory research project, not a clinically validated diagnostic assay.
